.Dd November 25, 2026
.Dt NVCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nvctl
.Nd headless NVIDIA GPU telemetry, power-cap, and persistence utility
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl jqv
.Op Fl d Ar index
.Op Ar command Op Ar subcommand Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility communicates directly with the NVIDIA Resource Manager (RM) kernel
interface via
.Pa /dev/nvidiactl
to query hardware telemetry, enforce runtime power caps, and maintain GPU
state persistence while no other process is accessing the device file.
.Pp
When invoked with no
.Ar command ,
.Nm
defaults to
.Cm status .
.Pp
The following global options are supported:
.Bl -tag -width "-d index"
.It Fl d Ar index
Operate only on the specified GPU device
.Ar index
(0-based).
By default, read-only commands iterate over all attached NVIDIA GPUs.
Mutating commands require
.Fl d
when more than one GPU is present.
.It Fl j
Emit machine-readable JSON output suitable for
.Ql node_exporter ,
dashboards, or external BMC controllers.
.It Fl q
Quiet / raw scalar mode for shell scripting (prints bare numeric values
without units or table headers).
.It Fl v
Enable human-readable RM diagnostics on
.Va stderr .
May be specified twice
.Pq Fl vv
for raw RM ioctl hex word dumps.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "power set watts"
.It Cm status
Display a summary table of all attached GPUs including index, RM
.Va gpuId ,
core temperature, hardware slowdown/shutdown thresholds, and active power
cap bounds (min/current/default/max watts).
This is the default command.
.It Cm list
Enumerate all attached NVIDIA GPUs and display their device node
.Pq Pa /dev/nvidia Ns Ar N ,
PCI bus/device/function address, RM
.Va gpuId ,
and model name.
.It Cm temp
Query on-die GPU thermal sensor along with hardware slowdown and emergency
shutdown thresholds.
.It Cm power Op Cm get
Display the active power cap and hardware minimum, default, and maximum
power limits in watts.
.It Cm power set Ar watts
Set the runtime GPU power limit to
.Ar watts
(validated against hardware min/max bounds and converted to milliwatts).
Requires root privileges.
Because
.Fx
resets GPU state to VBIOS defaults when the last open client closes
.Pa /dev/nvidia Ns Ar N ,
run
.Nm Cm persist
in the background to keep the power cap sticky across idle periods.
.It Cm persist
Hold
.Pa /dev/nvidiactl
and all present
.Pa /dev/nvidia Ns Ar N
device nodes open while sleeping at zero CPU usage in
.Xr pause 3
until
.Dv SIGINT
or
.Dv SIGTERM
is received, performing clean RM teardown on exit.
.It Cm probe
Perform a read-only RM ioctl capability probe across thermal, PMGR, and fan
control commands (combine with
.Fl vv
for raw non-zero word dumps).
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/dev/nvidiactl" -compact
.It Pa /dev/nvidiactl
NVIDIA Resource Manager control device.
.It Pa /dev/nvidia Ns Ar N
Per-GPU NVIDIA device nodes (numbered to match
.Ql vgapci
unit indices).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width "3" -compact
.It Li 0
Command completed successfully.
.It Li 1
System call, device open, or RM runtime error.
.It Li 2
Invalid command-line syntax, argument value, or out-of-bounds power cap.
.It Li 3
Requested operation is unsupported or gated by the RM driver or GPU
.Pq Dv NV_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED ;
no GPU state was modified.
.It Li 4
Driver accepted the write and updated GPU state, but clamped the applied
value away from the requested target.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Display a status summary for all GPUs:
.Pp
.Dl "nvctl"
.Pp
Print raw core temperature of GPU 0 for scripting:
.Pp
.Dl "nvctl -q -d 0 temp"
.Pp
Keep GPU state resident and cap GPU 0 to 150 watts:
.Pp
.Dl "nvctl persist &"
.Dl "sudo nvctl -d 0 power set 150"
.Pp
Dump full telemetry in JSON format:
.Pp
.Dl "nvctl -j status"
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pciconf 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An sumirati@buggycode.net
